# FOMO Store Environment Variables Template
# NEVER commit secret-bearing .env* files to source control or expose service_role / sb_secret_ keys.
#
# RECOMMENDED ISOLATION SETUP:
# 1. Keep root .env absent so Vite never falls back to Production during local dev or staging.
# 2. For Staging (`npm run dev:staging` / `npm run build:staging`), create `.env.staging`:
VITE_APP_ENV=staging
VITE_STAGING_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-staging-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_STAGING_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-staging-anon-public-key-here

# Optional: Specify your Production Supabase project ref (the 20-char subdomain of your prod URL)
# so Staging/Dev mode fails closed if someone accidentally pastes the Production URL into .env.staging:
VITE_PRODUCTION_PROJECT_REF=your-production-project-ref

# 3. For Production (`npm run dev:production` / `npm run build:production`), use `.env.production.local`:
# VITE_APP_ENV=production
# VITE_PRODUCTION_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-production-project-id.supabase.co
# VITE_PRODUCTION_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-production-anon-public-key-here
